<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajasthan Day</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">30 March 1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> Day is a public holiday in the Indian state of Rajasthan, celebrated on 30 March. It commemorates the inauguration in 1949 of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-state-of-greater-rajasthan">United State of Greater Rajasthan</a>, when the major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>, Bikaner and Jaisalmer joined the union, the decisive step in the formation of the present state.</p></div>
